        "Content": "Robin Hill, Lake Road, Cobh, Co. Cork, P24 RY88\r\n€950,000 Guide Price\r\n\r\nRobin Hill House is a truly exceptional Victorian residence occupying an elevated position on Lake Road in Rushbrooke, with magnificent southerly views across Cork Harbour. Dating from 1866 and designed by renowned architect Henry Hill, this landmark property combines remarkable period character, substantial accommodation and mature private grounds with enormous potential for both residential and commercial use.\r\nExtending to approximately 498 sq. m. (5,360 sq. ft.), Robin Hill stands on approximately 0.6 acre of mature, terraced gardens. The overall property provides an impressive nine bedrooms and eight bathrooms, comprising the substantial six-bedroom main residence, a separate two-bedroom apartment and a detached one-bedroom wooden chalet. The main house also offers five generous reception rooms, providing exceptional flexibility for private, hospitality or wellness use.\r\nThe main house is rich in Victorian character, with impressive proportions, high ceilings, tall windows and a distinctive Gothic Revival entrance porch. The six bedrooms within the principal house are all en suite, while a selection of generous reception rooms provides excellent space for family living, entertaining or continued hospitality use.\r\nOne of the great strengths of Robin Hill is the flexibility of its accommodation. The recently refurbished two-bedroom apartment extends to approximately 97 sq. m. and has its own private courtyard, together with both internal and external access. Finished with a contemporary touch, it is ideal for extended family, staff, guests or independent accommodation. A selection of fixtures and fittings is included in the sale.\r\nWithin the grounds is a further one-bedroom detached wooden chalet, complete with a shower room, galley kitchen, living and dining area and external decking. Previously used as pet-friendly self-catering guest accommodation, it provides yet another versatile element to this unique property. There is also potential for a second chalet within the grounds, subject to planning permission.\r\nOutside, the mature gardens extend to approximately 0.6 acre and enjoy a wonderful southerly orientation. The elevated position takes full advantage of the panoramic Cork Harbour views, while mature trees provide an excellent degree of privacy. Arranged over a series of terraces, the grounds include a glasshouse, productive kitchen garden, garden shed and a selection of bespoke private seating areas, while the gardens provide a peaceful setting for guests, private functions and outdoor entertaining.\r\nThe property also benefits from private parking for more than 12 vehicles, together with a garage, utility and storage space. The basement is divided into three areas and has previously been used as a wine cellar, offering further scope for storage or alternative use. These are unusual and particularly valuable features for a period property of this scale.\r\nRobin Hill has a fascinating history. Originally built as a substantial private residence, it later became a Church of Ireland rectory, known as The Parsonage, before returning to private ownership and subsequently developing into an established hospitality property.\r\nIn more recent years, Robin Hill has operated as a four-star Fáilte Ireland-approved guesthouse and holistic treatment centre, with the gardens also having hosted private functions and intimate weddings. The property is commercially licensed and is being offered for sale as a going concern, presenting an exciting opportunity for a purchaser wishing to continue or further develop a boutique hospitality, wellness or retreat business.\r\nEqually, Robin Hill could make an extraordinary private family residence. The scale of the main house, combined with the independent apartment and chalet, lends itself particularly well to multi-generational living, accommodation for extended family, guests or staff.\r\nSituated in Rushbrooke, the property enjoys a private and established setting while remaining conveniently positioned for Cobh town centre and its many amenities. Rail and bus connections are within easy reach, while Cork City and Cork Airport are approximately a 30-minute drive away.\r\nOffered with freehold title, Robin Hill House represents a rare opportunity to acquire a landmark Cork Harbour property where history, architecture, magnificent views, extensive accommodation and exceptional versatility come together in one remarkable offering.\r\n\r\nKey Features\r\n•\tApprox. 498 sq. m. / 5,360 sq. ft.\r\n•\tApprox. 0.6 acre of mature private grounds\r\n•\t9 bedrooms and 8 bathrooms overall\r\n•\tMain residence with 6 en-suite bedrooms\r\n•\tSeparate 2-bedroom apartment\r\n•\tDetached 1-bedroom wooden chalet\r\n•\tMagnificent southerly Cork Harbour views\r\n•\tDesigned by architect Henry Hill\r\n•\tBeautiful Victorian character and proportions\r\n•\tMature terraced gardens and glasshouse\r\n•\tGarage and basement storage\r\n•\tPrivate parking for 12+ vehicles\r\n•\tFour-star Fáilte Ireland-approved guesthouse history\r\n•\tExcellent private residence, hospitality or wellness potential\r\n•\tFive generous reception rooms\r\n•\tCommercially licensed property offered as a going concern\r\n•\tTwo-bedroom apartment extending to approx. 97 sq. m.\r\n•\tSelection of fixtures and fittings included\r\n•\tWine cellar\r\n•\tKitchen garden, glasshouse and garden shed\r\n•\tPotential for a second chalet, subject to planning permission\r\n•\tFreehold title\r\n•\tBER Exempt"
      },
